I recently ascended a Ranger. Nothing spectacular besides this
curious bones, so I may or may not write a YAAP later.

I entered the Minetown with my early-game ranger. The town was
the "large" one this time, the one with the Gnome King's statue
in it etc.

Near the lower right end of the screen I found a tombstone,
with the words "Gaynor, killed by choking on a yeti corpse."
I think it was Gaynor the tourist who had died. IIRC, I had
polymorphed into a water troll and tried to eat a yeti
corpse in order to get cold resistance... while satiated.
Hey, if I die in polymorphed form, it doesn't really matter.
Except that it did.

Months later, after having forgotten this event, my knight
Zan wandered in the same town where Gaynor had perished.
Soon, near the foodstore, a water troll appears and bests
me in a short and a glorious fight. Now, why would there
be water trolls in gnometown? Some foo polytrapped above
the town and dropped through hole? Some foo quaffed a
!oPoly? Or was the water troll ex-Gaynor the tourist?

Anyway, I soon forgot the incident until I found the
double bones in the Gnome Town with my ranger.
Yeah, there's Gaynor's tomb and "Zan, killed by a water
troll." I zapped the troll with /oSleep and shot it dead
with my bow. The troll never regenerated. It was also
unnamed. Darn, I can't remember whether or not I ever
encountered Gaynor's ghost for sure!

So, here's what I'm thinking what happened: Gaynor,
polymorphed into water troll, died and left a water troll
corpse behind which regenerated. Nobody was there to see
whether or not the _corpse_ was named or not if a corpse
indeed was left. Probably not...
Later the water troll killed Zan, creating a double
bones level which my ranger discovered.


